{
  "id": "classical-test-theory",
  "term": "classical test theory",
  "definition": "Classical test theory is a measurement approach that uses the idea of a true score: a theoretical, error-free value underlying a person’s test performance. In this framework, repeated scores on parallel forms can average toward that true score because random error tends to cancel out.",
